.TH ALX-ASSISTANT 1 "November 2026" "Algothix OS (ALX) Lite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alx-assistant \- optional cloud-API AI desktop assistant for Algothix OS (ALX) Lite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alx-assistant
[\fB\-\-setup\fR | \fB\-\-source\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR | \fB\-\-panic\-stop\fR | \fB\-\-type\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alx-assistant
launches the optional ALX Assistant desktop application on X11 (Awesome WM).
It requires an internet connection and the user's own cloud model API key
(Gemini, Claude, or ChatGPT). No network requests are made until a key is
configured.
.PP
Safe defaults are enforced on initialization:
.BR allowActions=false ,
.BR skipAllow=false ,
.BR rawReadOnly=true ,
and
.BR telemetry=false .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Run the first-run terminal setup wizard (\fBalx-assistant-setup\fR) to choose a
provider, store your API key securely, and set an optional notes folder.
.TP
.B \-\-source
Print the AGPL-3.0 corresponding source repository URL and pinned upstream
commit SHA.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print current assistant state (\fBoff\fR, \fBlistening\fR, or \fBactions\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-panic\-stop
Immediately terminate any running ALX Assistant and sidecar processes and reset
state to \fBoff\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-type
Launch or focus ALX Assistant in text prompt mode.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/alx-assistant/settings.json
User configuration (mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.config/alx-assistant/hotkeys.env
Configurable Awesome WM hotkey bindings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/alx-assistant/SOURCE
AGPL-3.0 corresponding source offer and commit pin.
